Subject: [PATCH 2/3] x86/i8237: skip legacy DMA init under the Composite VMM

The Composite simple_vmm does not emulate the legacy 8237 DMA controller. On a
normal machine i8237A_init_ops() pokes the DMA controller's I/O ports; under the
VMM those accesses have no backing device.

Return early so the init op becomes a no-op inside the guest.

This is a device-emulation gap workaround, not a kernel bug fix: it should be
revisited if the VMM ever grows legacy DMA emulation.

---
--- a/arch/x86/kernel/i8237.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/i8237.c
@@ -47,6 +47,8 @@
 
 static int __init i8237A_init_ops(void)
 {
+	/* VMM doesn't support this in the VM, doesn't matter */
+	return 0;
 	/*
 	 * From SKL PCH onwards, the legacy DMA device is removed in which the
 	 * I/O ports (81h-83h, 87h, 89h-8Bh, 8Fh) related to it are removed
